 \tag{R3}\] for \(n-j\) even, and zero otherwise. This follows from the Gaussian binomial count of \(j\)-subspaces and the number of nondegenerate alternating forms; the power of two simplifies to \(-j(j-1)/2\). Exact enumeration for every \(n\le5\) agrees with (R3).

