 =\frac1{4r}\int_{\partial D_r}
 \left(\frac{2V(u_\varepsilon)}{\varepsilon}
       +\varepsilon|u_r|^2-\varepsilon|u_\tau|^2\right).\] No positivity at fixed \(\varepsilon\) is assumed. Once Proposition 1.20 supplies the absolutely continuous discrepancy relation, rotation of the quadratic tensor gives \(N^{\rm ac}_{x_0,\star}=4\sin^2(\gamma_\star-\theta)\zeta_\star^{\rm ac}\ge0\), as in Lemma 9.1.

There is a second elementary obstruction in the exact norm used for the initial data. At \(v_\varepsilon=(1/(2\varepsilon),0,0)\), the cutoff is one and the difference is exactly \(\varepsilon\), whence \[\|f^\varepsilon(0)-f_0\|_{L^\infty_k}
 \geq \varepsilon\langle v_\varepsilon\rangle^k
 \geq 2^{-k}\varepsilon^{1-k}.\] It diverges for every \(k>1\), in particular for the weights used by Theorem 2.1. The energy divergence in [energy] (#energy) also prevents using the cited mass/energy-dependent estimates uniformly by simply invoking that theorem.

The Euler cancellation on pp. 121–122 is \[\sum_{s=r}^{k}(-1)^{s-1}\binom{k-r}{s-r}
 =
 \begin{cases}0,&r<k,\\(-1)^{k-1},&r=k.\end{cases}\] The endpoint simplifications on pp. 122–123 and 133–134 were checked with parity and congruences retained. Independent enumeration tested 249,510 bounded tuples for the former simplification and 2,250 even-generator endpoint cases without mismatch; the bounds are recorded in the script. This does not verify the full Bredon spectral sequence or matching theorem.

