 =\cos\theta\,I+\sin\theta\,J.\] The field is stationary and has finite range of dependence in the probabilistic sense, since its law is deterministic. Moreover \(\left\lVert g_\theta\right\rVert\le h\), so the weak \(\Gamma_2\) bound (D.26) holds for every \(\theta\) with the same \(h\). Now \(\operatorname{sym}\mathbf a_\theta=\cos\theta\,I>0\), and the constant field belongs to \(\Omega\).

