 \frac{\Gamma(d/2-\alpha)}
 {4^\alpha\pi^{d/2}\Gamma(\alpha)}
 |x|^{2\alpha-d}\] be the heat-potential kernel from (D.13). The definition immediately before (D.22) integrates a heat convolution with \(\eta_n\); its white-noise kernel is \(k_\alpha*\eta_n\), not the pointwise product \(k_\alpha\eta_n\) written in (D.22). For a nonzero nonnegative smooth annular cutoff, \(k_\alpha*\eta_n\) is strictly positive everywhere and lies in \(L^2\). Its covariance with every translate is strictly positive. The resulting stationary Gaussian field has no finite dependence range. The product kernel, in contrast, is compactly supported. Thus the printed identity does not establish the required property.

