 \end{pmatrix}\right|=3.\] Its only lattice points are its four vertices: an integral height in \([0,1]\) is zero or one, and both face segments are primitive. A triangulation using lattice vertices cannot subdivide this empty tetrahedron further, so it cannot be unimodular. This also disproves the relevant two-factor version of (A) with the literal ambient lattice.

