 \asymp r^{-n/(q-n+1-\beta)},\] or by two exponential bounds retaining constants inside their exponents. Composing with the logarithmic \(\varphi\) then gives the claimed final power. The displayed \(J(s)\) asymptotics on pp. 14–15 concern \(s\to0\), so their near-infinity labels should also be corrected. This is a false intermediate comparison with an explicit corrected derivation, not a refutation of Example 3.9’s final conclusion.

