Let \(E_\mathbb Q=\mathbb Qe_0\oplus\mathbb Qe_1\). Define \[W_mE_\mathbb Q=\begin{cases}
 0&m<-2,\\ \mathbb Qe_1&-2\le m<0,\\ E_\mathbb Q&m\ge0,
 \end{cases}
 \qquad
 F^pE_\mathbb C=\begin{cases}
 0&p\ge1,\\
 \mathbb C(e_0+i e_1)&p=0,\\
 E_\mathbb C&p\le-1 .
 \end{cases}\] The induced graded pieces are of types \((-1,-1)\) and \((0,0)\). They are rank-one Tate structures and admit polarizations. Thus \(E\) is a graded-polarizable mixed Hodge structure, in the standard meaning of the target category; see the separately consulted [Retained latex: \cite[Example 1.4(ii), p.~9]{Drew}], which also records homological dimension one in Remark 1.5(ii).

