Problem 2 (A conditional discrepancy in the critical-range calculation).  Lemma 3.6, p. 18, lists the critical integers of \(L(\operatorname{Sym}^2M(f),s)\) as \[\{n\text{ odd}:\lambda_1+1\le n\le w\}
 \ \cup\
 \{n\text{ even}:w+1\le n\le\lambda_1+2\lambda_2\}.\] Its displayed Gamma factor requires an additional restriction when \(2\lambda_2>\lambda_1\). Realization of a proposed numerical witness by a form satisfying all arithmetic hypotheses is assessed separately below.

Set \(M=\max(\lambda_1,2\lambda_2)\). The four complex factors \[\Gamma_{\mathbb C}(s)\Gamma_{\mathbb C}(s-\lambda_2)
 \Gamma_{\mathbb C}(s-2\lambda_2)\Gamma_{\mathbb C}(s-\lambda_1)\] are regular at the integer \(s=n\) exactly when \(n\ge M+1\). Self-duality of weight \(2w\) requires regularity also at \(2w+1-n\), hence \[M+1\le n\le 2w-M=\min(2\lambda_1,\lambda_1+2\lambda_2).\] The real factor \(\Gamma_{\mathbb R}(s+1-w)^2\), with \(w\) odd, permits odd \(n\) on the lower side and even \(n\) on the upper side. Consequently the exact replacement is \[\boxed{\;
 \{n\text{ odd}:M+1\le n\le w\}
 \ \cup\
 \{n\text{ even}:w+1\le n\le2w-M\}.
 \;}\] For the parameter pair \((34,33)\) only \(67,68\) remain. The retained independent exact integer-pole calculation reproduces this result and cross-checks the general formula on a bounded grid; the proof is the preceding Gamma analysis, not that finite enumeration.

