Equation reference: eq:control. Theorem 4.3 states that if \(a\in S^0_{1,0}(T^*M)\) is independent of \(h\) and \(\{a\ne0\}\cap S^*M\) is \(V^+\)-dense and \(V^-\)-dense, there are constants \(C,h_0>0\), depending on \(M,a\), such that \[
 \|u\|_{L^2}
 \le C\|\operatorname{Op}_h(a)u\|_{L^2}
   +\frac{C\log(1/h)}{h}\|(-h^2\Delta_g-I)u\|_{L^2}
 \quad (u\in H^2(M),\ 0<h\le h_0).\] The following verifies its application to Theorem 1.3, conditional on this estimate and Theorem 3.3.

Assessment: Minor, local formula error. On p. 15 the final term of (56) is printed as \[(1-r)^{-3}\frac{d}{dt}\mathbb EA_t^2 .\] Since \(\Gamma_r=A_t/(1-r)\) and \(t=r/(1-r)\), the chain rule requires \[\frac{d}{dr}\mathbb E\Gamma_r
 =\frac{\mathbb E\Gamma_r}{1-r}
  +\frac{1}{(1-r)^3}\frac{d}{dt}\mathbb EA_t .\] This distinction is substantive for the displayed equality: for standard Gaussian initial data, \(A_t=(1+t)^{-1}\mathrm{Id}\) and \(\Gamma_r=\mathrm{Id}\). The derivative is zero, whereas the printed right-hand side at \(r=1/4\) equals \(-2\mathrm{Id}/3\).

Lemma 3.1 gives \(q(\xi)\le4m/(1-\xi)^2\). Consequently, \[\int_\xi^1 q(r)\,dr
 \le \left(\frac{32}{\xi^2}
          +\frac{16}{\xi(1-\xi)}\right)m .\] Monotonicity of \(q\) gives \(\int_0^1q\le(1-\xi)^{-1}\int_\xi^1q\). By Corollary 3.2, \[\frac{D(\mu\Vert\gamma_1)}m\le B,\qquad
 B=\frac{16}{\xi^2(1-\xi)}
   +\frac{8}{\xi(1-\xi)^2}.\] The entropy normalization therefore yields \[L_n\le c_p^{-1}L_\mu
       \le \frac{c_p^{-1}e^B}{\sqrt{2\pi e}}
       \qquad(n\ge10).\] This is dimension-free; all entropy expressions use the selected dimension \(m\). The finitely many smaller dimensions are absorbed in the constant. No numerical value is asserted for the universal input constants.

