 \left(\frac{\mathcal E(x_k)+\eta}{\alpha}\right)^{1/\beta}
 \le(2\varepsilon_k/\alpha)^{1/\beta}.\] The next call is valid. Its output may fall below the noise floor; the validity premise is needed at its input, not again after this final successful call. Greedy selection prevents later interleaving from increasing \(\mathcal E\). If the target is below \(\eta\), attaining \(\eta\) suffices; if \(\eta\ge\varepsilon_0\), the initial point already meets the target. These checks support the combined-error conclusion rather than an off-by-one objection.

